TimeFlowExtrafieldsDisabled = This page is disabled: TimeEntry does not manage extra fields (isextrafieldmanaged is off), so any field defined here would never appear on a time entry and its value would never be saved.
TIMEFLOW_LATE_ALERT_ENABLED = Morning late-arrival alerts
TIMEFLOW_LATE_ALERT_ENABLED_TOOLTIP = Detects each morning the employees who started no timer before the cut-off time and warns the users who have the "Read all time entries" right (TimeFlow notification, and email according to their preference). Off by default. Needs the Scheduled jobs (cron) module active and running.
TIMEFLOW_LATE_THRESHOLD_TIME = Arrival threshold time
TIMEFLOW_LATE_THRESHOLD_TIME_TOOLTIP = Time (HH:MM, server time) before which a timer must have been started. Default 09:00.
TIMEFLOW_LATE_GRACE_MINUTES = Tolerance (minutes)
TIMEFLOW_LATE_GRACE_MINUTES_TOOLTIP = Minutes allowed after the threshold time before an employee is considered late. The cut-off is threshold + tolerance. Default 10.
TIMEFLOW_LATE_WORKDAYS = Days checked
TIMEFLOW_LATE_WORKDAYS_TOOLTIP = Days of the week on which the detection runs. No public-holiday calendar is known: a day on which nobody started a timer is treated as a non-working day.
TIMEFLOW_LATE_MAX_DELAY_HOURS = Maximum detection delay (hours)
TIMEFLOW_LATE_MAX_DELAY_HOURS_TOOLTIP = If the first run of the day happens more than this many hours after the cut-off (server down, cron not running), no alert is sent that day. Default 3.
TIMEFLOW_LATE_ACTIVE_WINDOW_DAYS = Recent activity window (days)
TIMEFLOW_LATE_ACTIVE_WINDOW_DAYS_TOOLTIP = Only active accounts that started at least one timer during this period are monitored (an old account that was never disabled is not "late" every morning). Default 30.
